    {
      "kind": "prose",
      "text": "The near-unity unconditional relative difference is driven by **W186** in the\nproduct, where both codes predict essentially zero but with different numerical\nfloor values (Nucleide \u2248 3.20e-14, PyNE \u2248 2.74e-12). When looking only at\nnuclides whose reference fraction exceeds 1e-6, the largest relative mismatch\nis **W184** (\u2248 88% relative) and **W183** (\u2248 64% relative) \u2014 these minor-isotope\ndifferences are expected because Nucleide is run here with a fixed `M*` while\nPyNE optimizes `M*`."
    },
